## Summary

Add a manual, budgeted live-acceptance surface without putting Jules mutations into ordinary CI.

## Changes

- add opt-in read-only, repoless lifecycle, and source-backed lifecycle probes;
- require `JULES_LIVE_TEST=1` and explicit task budget for every mutating probe;
- clean up created sessions in `finally` blocks;
- avoid automatic PR creation and repository edits in the baseline source probe;
- add a protected-environment `workflow_dispatch` with read-only, repoless, or source modes;
- register the `live` pytest marker so ordinary CI skips these probes cleanly.

## Important limit

This PR adds the harness but does not run it. No Jules credential is available to this development session, so authenticated acceptance remains unearned until the protected workflow is configured and invoked.

## Objetivo

Aplicar la decisión supervisora del PR #130: ejecutar la preparación privada exclusivamente en un runner autoalojado de la máquina de Ana.

Relates #45. El Issue #43 permanece abierto.

## Configuración viva verificada

- runner de repositorio `enares-stage04-local`: online;
- etiquetas: `self-hosted`, `Windows`, `X64`, `stage04-private-input`;
- arranque automático bajo la sesión local de Ana;
- inbox local con ACL restringida al usuario;
- Environment `stage04-shadow-mutation`: Rita es la única revisora requerida;
- `prevent_self_review`: activo;
- política de despliegue: solamente `main`.

## Cambio versionado

- el workflow deja `ubuntu-latest` y exige las cuatro etiquetas del runner aprobado;
- pasos shell convertidos a PowerShell para Windows;
- el nombre real del CSV se deriva de `manifest.file_name` y se valida como basename seguro;
- hook de inicio copia desde el inbox local después de que GitHub limpia `RUNNER_TEMP`;
- hook final elimina las copias del inbox y del temporal;
- solo la evidencia redactada puede subirse como artifact;
- el workflow todavía termina antes de carga, consulta, promoción o cualquier mutación cloud.

GitHub documenta que `RUNNER_TEMP` se vacía al inicio y al final de cada job. Por eso no era correcto depositar allí el archivo antes del disparo; el hook posterior a la limpieza conserva el propósito exacto de la decisión sin introducir bucket, secreto, Release, URL, artifact previo ni sincronización con Drive.

## Verificación

- prueba local de hooks con copia del agregado autorizado: `HOOK_TEST=PASS`;
- suite: `487 passed, 2 skipped`;
- ruff: limpio;
- mypy: limpio, 86 archivos;
- `git diff --check`: limpio;
- sin datos, credenciales, IDs privados ni rutas personales en el diff;
- mutaciones cloud y cargas reales: 0.

## Gate

Solicito Review changes → Approve de @ritaricaldi-cpu sobre este SHA. Después del merge se podrá realizar una corrida supervisada de preparación; el job cloud de carga/reconciliación seguirá en un PR posterior y consumirá el Environment protegido.

## Summary

Adds the detailed implementation plan for the reviewed Docker-first Local Development Environment design now landed on `main`.

## Scope

Planning only. This PR contains exactly one plan file relative to `main`; no Compose topology, Dockerfile, runtime source, CI implementation, migration, contract, or product code is introduced.

## Plan structure

The plan remains split into seven reviewable tasks:

1. repository-owned local-dev change detection;
2. static Docker-foundation fitness checks;
3. generic placeholder image + canonical Compose topology;
4. isolated Compose smoke verification including persistence/reset;
5. canonical local-development documentation;
6. path-aware CI integration under stable `CI / gate`;
7. final implementation PR and ordered landing verification.

## Reviewed-design alignment

PR #9 external review produced four design corrections, all propagated into this plan:

- configured database inspection uses `POSTGRES_USER` / `POSTGRES_DB`;
- PostgreSQL first-initialization behavior and destructive reset semantics are explicit;
- parallel worktree isolation requires distinct resolved Compose project names;
- static topology verification now requires explicit PostgreSQL/placeholder healthchecks and negative healthcheck fixtures.

Task 2 therefore pins **19** topology cases instead of the prior 16.

## Current implementation inputs

- Docker Compose floor: `>= 2.22.0`;
- PostgreSQL: `postgres:18.6-alpine3.24`;
- placeholder base: `alpine:3.24.2`.

## Self-review evidence

- exactly seven implementation tasks;
- plan branch is rebased/restacked directly on reviewed `main`;
- main-to-plan diff contains only one plan file;
- no runtime/application implementation leakage;
- reviewed design findings are mapped to Task 2 and Task 5 verification;
- aggregate `CI / gate` semantics remain unchanged.

## Stack state

- PR #9 design: merged to `main`;
- PR #10 plan: this PR, base `main`;
- PR #11 implementation: remains downstream and must be reconciled to this reviewed plan before landing.

## Implementation status

The implementation branch/PR already exists because this plan was explicitly approved and executed task-by-task. Landing remains review-gated; implementation will not be merged until this reviewed plan lands and PR #11 is updated to match it.

Advances #1050 and #986 with the first non-colliding symbolic/programmable Org automation slice.

## What
- adds a parser-neutral `OrgAutomationHeading` projection consumed from the canonical Org parser/storage authority;
- compiles ordinary Org `WHEN` / optional `IF` / ordered `THEN` sections into inert typed symbol references;
- requires stable Org `ID`, bounded declarative selectors, deterministic semantic hashing, and preserves unknown root properties as inert metadata;
- preserves arbitrary user roots/workspaces: source paths are provenance only and this layer has no `Documents/Notes/org` default;
- inspects trigger/condition/action symbols through an injected canonical #986 descriptor lookup rather than creating a second symbol registry;
- surfaces required capabilities, owner, kind, availability and platform support without granting authority or invoking anything;
- fails closed for missing/unavailable/platform-incompatible symbols;
- rejects synced recipe fields that try to embed shell, raw Intent, Python eval, Prolog goals, class names, filesystem/plugin-registry or other ambient execution mechanisms.

## Authority boundary
This PR deliberately owns **no** raw Org parser, editor, index, sync engine, scheduler, command registry, approval store, filesystem access or executor. Ordinary Org remains canonical. The canonical Org layer supplies heading projections; the canonical #986 registry supplies symbol descriptors; later runtime wiring must execute through existing typed capability/principal/approval authority.

A recipe reference never grants permission. Inspection only surfaces canonical capability requirements; there is intentionally no automation-local grant/approval bit or execution method.

## RED first
`d94922fa38a2531ccb8d21e3c1754bc06cc18646` added the initial contract regressions before `zara.org_automation` existed. Implementation followed in `47b5f5204901f88727c2599b72960498eba9bb6c`.

A second RED-first authority refinement at `bbd1b2fd56274588777c17324125d807e97f92d6` removed the bespoke automation-safety flag from the expected API; `8e451568d3971df03f21bac45d30c87df26600eb` follows by leaving authorization wholly to the canonical capability/principal/approval runtime.

Coverage includes arbitrary source roots, metadata preservation, deterministic definition hashes, ordered multiple actions, raw-authority injection negatives, malformed recipe shape, inspect-without-execute, missing/unavailable symbols, capability-only authority projection, platform mismatch and disabled recipes.

## Reconciliation
The existing branch is merge-forwarded onto `master@5b2fc85f7f49b078a8ae612719ed17ab8b01e937` at exact head `b14deb8618ed7272bd25efd1337cd9f65e7a1af3`. The reconciliation preserves current-master Android/dotfiles/evidence changes and changelog content plus this PR's Org automation entry. Compare is 0 behind master and the PR delta remains exactly three files: the automation contract, its focused tests, and one changelog line.

## Gate
Draft until exact-head CI is terminal-green. Missing/pending/stale/skipped/cancelled checks are not green. Fresh exact-head CI run `35423851796` is in progress after reconciliation. The previous exact head `154cb24b1aa7cb407f56b42877f6d34810ae6671` was **not green**: the main test phase passed, but `nix flake check` failed and Android screenshot evidence failed before terminal success. Current master CI for `5b2fc85f7f49b078a8ae612719ed17ab8b01e937` is green; this branch still must prove its own exact head. This slice has no UI change and therefore does not claim new Android/Desktop screenshot evidence.

