## Goal

Treat the published Docker images as software distribution artifacts and ship a
clear open-source acknowledgment/copyright document with each runtime profile.

Use a maintained plain-text source as the authoring input and generate a PDF
from that same source during the image build.

## Required release contract

- canonical authoring input: `compliance/OPEN_SOURCE_ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.txt`;
- generated runtime outputs:
  - `/usr/share/doc/scad-toolchain/OPEN_SOURCE_ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.txt`;
  - `/usr/share/doc/scad-toolchain/OPEN_SOURCE_ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.pdf`;
- generated package inventories for the actual image contents;
- explicit references to the license/copyright material already distributed in
  the image for Ubuntu packages, Python distributions and bundled CAD
  libraries;
- build/smoke tests must fail if the acknowledgment outputs are missing or the
  PDF is malformed;
- expose the document paths through `scad-toolchain-info`;
- document the distribution/compliance boundary in README/AGENTS.

The PDF generator should use only the Python standard library so generating the
acknowledgment does not introduce another runtime dependency that itself needs
to be licensed.

## Version

Prepare this as the next immutable toolchain release, `v0.5.2`.

## Qualification

Follow the normal release gate:

1. PR owner build/smoke green;
2. main/edge build green;
3. external consumer suite against edge green with acknowledgment coverage;
4. release exact main as v0.5.2;
5. exact v0.5.2 images + external suite green;
6. create matching immutable external test-suite record;
7. only then advance downstream consumers.

