Everything from `if (sg < 2) {` onward — the `simd_sum(acc)`, the
`metal::precise::rsqrt`, the `q_shared`/`k_shared`/`v_shared` writes, the
`conv_out` copy guarded by `sg == 2 || hv_idx % (Hv / Hk) == 0`, the gate and
decay block, the row loop, the gated-RMS epilogue — is untouched. The `win`
lambda is retained because the `conv_out` copy still uses it.

## Why every value is identical

| quantity | shipped | after |
|---|---|---|
| channel a lane folds | `vec * 128 + lane * 4 + i`, `i` in `0..3` | `vecA * 128 + lane * 4 + ii`, `ii = sg & 3`, the same four channels per lane across the four simdgroups of that vector |
| tap fold | `cacc += win(j, ch) * conv_w[ch * KC + j]`, `j` ascending | same expression, same ascending `j`; the `win` branch is written out as the same `j < KM1` test |
| operand types | `float * InT` (InT promotes) | same |
| `c0`, `c1` | `static_cast<InT>(cacc)`, `mlx_silu(c0)` | same |
| what `thread_x[i]` holds | `static_cast<float>(c1)` | the same value, routed through a `float` threadgroup slot |
| `acc` | `acc += thread_x[i] * thread_x[i]`, `i` ascending, one lane | same lane, same four values, same ascending order |
| `simd_sum(acc)` | the 32 lanes of simdgroup `sg` | unchanged |
| `inv_mean`, `q_mul`, `k_mul`, `normalized` | — | unchanged |

`float` threadgroup memory stores and reloads the value exactly, so the
hand-off is lossless.

## Cost

`xs_shared` adds `3 * Dk` floats = 1536 B of threadgroup memory, on top of the
existing `q_shared`/`k_shared`/`v_shared` (768 B at `InT` = bfloat16),
`gb_shared` (8 B) and `y_shared` (256 B). One extra
`threadgroup_barrier(mem_flags::mem_threadgroup)` is added before the reduction
phase.

Per participating thread the tap fold covers one channel rather than four.

