Changes:
- replaces the old single-uniform-point dense conclusion on README and Pages with the entropy-sweep conclusion;
- states that dense leads interactive only under uniform access, while interactive overtakes it between about 12 and 8 bits of access entropy and keeps the lead through H_alpha ≈ 2;
- adds the measured single-request loop loss: BGZF's advantage over ACEAPEX interactive grows from ~1.1x under uniform to ~4.7x near H_alpha ≈ 2;
